  "tcp": {
    "status": "unresolved",
    "facts": [
      "The official URDF defines no tool0 or dedicated TCP frame; the deepest tool-flange link is link6.",
      "The fork uses EE_Frames=['link6'] in config/user_config.json, so IK targets land on link6, not on a documented TCP.",
      "The pinned submodule adds flange_link (identity from link6) and gripper_base (+0.0045 m from flange_link), but no TCP frame is declared in either variant.",
      "Finger frames are prismatic, so a finger-midpoint TCP would move with the gripper command and is not defined anywhere official.",
      "Manipulation offsets in config/user_config.json (Grasp_TCP_Top_Offset=-0.0053 m, Gripper_Open_Clearance, Pregrasp_Clearance) are locally tuned values, not documented official TCP parameters.",
      "Distance from link6 to the finger contact surfaces differs between the robot_assets snapshot (0.1358 m finger origin) and the pinned submodule (0.0045 + 0.138 m), so a link6-referenced grasp offset cannot be validated against a single official number yet."
    ],
    "resolution_target": "Resolve before P1 grasp execution work."
  },
